      "description": "DRAFT lane. Same TaoMate 3-step image-to-video shot, rendered at half width and height and decoded at 2x by the X2 Detail VAE. Measured on a DGX Spark (GB10), 5 s at 768p output: 32-38 s per job with the VRAM unload steps on, as this pack ships (measured with a repeated prompt; a new prompt adds about 4 s). With both unload steps off it took 29-30 s with a new prompt each job, plus 6-16 s once after a restart, after another card ran, or when the LoRA set changes. The normal TaoMate preset took 112-120 s there. This card also sets the Comfy Kitchen attention backend, which the normal TaoMate card does not, so the gap is not from the decode alone. Words came out correct 4 of 4. COST: softer picture (edge strength 0.50-0.65x), eyes smear in fast eye motion. It is a DIFFERENT take from the normal preset on the same seed, so use it to check prompt, words and motion, not to pick the final take. The resolution label is the OUTPUT size. Tested only on a DGX Spark (GB10, 128 GB unified memory); 12-16 GB cards and 32-64 GB RAM PCs are untested.",
